## Changes to `src/c_cp/c_cp.c`

### 1. Add a `prompt_interactive` helper (place it just before `copy_path`)

```c
static int prompt_interactive(const char *dst) {
    fprintf(stderr, "override '%s'? ", dst);
    fflush(stderr);
    int c = getchar();
    int affirm = (c == 'y' || c == 'Y');
    int ch;
    while ((ch = getchar()) != EOF && ch != '\n') {}
    return affirm;
}
```

### 2. Modify `copy_path` signature and body

Change the signature from:
```c
static int copy_path(const char *src, const char *dst, int force) {
```
to:
```c
static int copy_path(const char *src, const char *dst, int force, int interactive) {
```

Insert the interactive check immediately after the "same file" check inside the `if (dst_existed) {` block, before the `int dstfd;` line. Add this block:

```c
        if (interactive) {
            if (!prompt_interactive(dst)) {
                close(srcfd);
                return 1;
            }
        }
```

The return-value contract becomes: `0` = success, `1` = skipped (interactive decline), `-1` = error.

### 3. Add `-i` / `--interactive` option parsing in `main`

Add a variable declaration next to `int force = 0;`:
```c
    int interactive = 0;
```

Inside the option-parsing loop, extend the recognized-options check from:
```c
            if (strcmp(argv[i], "-f") == 0 || strcmp(argv[i], "--force") == 0) {
                force = 1;
                continue;
            }
```
to:
```c
            if (strcmp(argv[i], "-f") == 0 || strcmp(argv[i], "--force") == 0) {
                force = 1;
                continue;
            }
            if (strcmp(argv[i], "-i") == 0 || strcmp(argv[i], "--interactive") == 0) {
                interactive = 1;
                continue;
            }
```

### 4. Update all `copy_path` call sites in `main` to pass `interactive`

There are three call sites. Change each from:
```c
copy_path(src, effective_dst, force)
```
to:
```c
copy_path(src, effective_dst, force, interactive)
```
and similarly for the non-directory-destination call:
```c
copy_path(src, dst, force, interactive)
```

### 5. Handle the "skipped" return value (1) at each call site

At each call site, the current pattern is:
```c
if (copy_path(src, effective_dst, force) == -1) {
    status = 1;
}
```
Change it to:
```c
int rc = copy_path(src, effective_dst, force, interactive);
if (rc != 0) {
    status = 1;
}
```
Do this at all three call sites (the two-operand non-directory case, the two-operand directory case, and the multi-source loop). This way both errors (`-1`) and interactive skips (`1`) contribute status 1, while only errors produce a diagnostic (which `copy_path` already prints internally).

---

### Summary of behavior implemented

- `-i` / `--interactive`: when the effective destination already exists as a regular file, a prompt is written to stderr, one line is read from stdin; only a first character of `y` or `Y` affirms. Decline (leading whitespace, empty line, EOF, any other first character) skips that copy, contributes exit status 1, and processing continues.
- `-f` / `--force` (already present): retained unchanged; force replacement still requires interactive confirmation when `-i` is also given.
- All other checkpoint-001 behavior is preserved.
